        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "apparently you are using the snap build? `/snap/nvim/4813/` would be good to mention that.\n\nif you run `ruff server` does it work? inside/outside nvim? try this:\n\n```lua\nvim.lsp.set_log_level('trace')\n\nvim.lsp.start({\n  name = 'ruff-minimal',\n  cmd = { 'ruff', 'server' },\n  root_dir = vim.uv.cwd(),\n  on_init = function(client, result)\n    print('ON_INIT', vim.inspect(result))\n  end,\n  on_exit = function(code, signal, client_id)\n    print('ON_EXIT', vim.inspect({\n      code = code,\n      signal = signal,\n      client_id = client_id,\n    }))\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nthen:\n\n```\n:lua dofile('/tmp/ruff-minimal.lua')\n:lua print(vim.lsp.get_log_path())\n```\n\nthis isn't an nvim bug anyway. `ruff quit with exit code 2` is Nvim telling you that ruff didn't work.",
